 \section{Limitations and Future Work}\label{sec:limits}
 %=====================================================================
-\emph{Emulators, not clouds.} All provider results come from moto, Azurite and \code{gcp-storage-emulator} on one host. Real IAM policies, latency, eventual-consistency effects and costs were not evaluated, and no TLS or reverse proxy was in the path. \emph{Single instance.} Rate limiting, lockout counters, health state and audit-append serialisation are per process; a distributed deployment needs shared state (the PostgreSQL advisory-lock path for the audit chain exists but is untested). \emph{Bearer tokens.} Access tokens are not bound to the client; DPoP~\cite{rfc9449} or mutual-TLS-bound tokens~\cite{rfc8705} would make a stolen token far less useful within its 5-minute lifetime. \emph{TOFU window.} Closing the enrolment window requires an out-of-band channel or enterprise identity federation. \emph{Erasure coding.} Reed--Solomon or IDA-style coding~\cite{rabin1989,bessani2011depsky} would lower storage overhead and give true dispersal, at the cost of complexity. \emph{Client-side encryption.} The backend sees plaintext and keys (non-goal~(ii)); end-to-end encryption in the client would remove this but complicates sharing, server-side verification and detection. \emph{HSM-backed KMS.} The local keystore should be replaced by an external KMS or HSM in production; an AWS KMS adapter exists but was exercised only against moto. Finally, timing side channels were not measured, no fuzzing beyond a hand-picked payload list was performed, and there are no React component tests.
+\emph{Emulators, not clouds.} All provider results come from moto, Azurite and \code{gcp-storage-emulator} on one host. Real IAM policies, latency, eventual-consistency effects and costs were not evaluated, and no TLS or reverse proxy was in the path. The chunk-size tuning of Section~\ref{sec:perf} was measured on one host with no network latency and up to 1\,GiB; on real links a large chunk is a larger retry unit, so the 30\,s provider deadline we pair with 16\,MiB chunks should be re-validated against real providers. \emph{Single instance.} Rate limiting, lockout counters, health state and audit-append serialisation are per process; a distributed deployment needs shared state (the PostgreSQL advisory-lock path for the audit chain exists but is untested). \emph{Bearer tokens.} Access tokens are not bound to the client; DPoP~\cite{rfc9449} or mutual-TLS-bound tokens~\cite{rfc8705} would make a stolen token far less useful within its 5-minute lifetime. \emph{TOFU window.} Closing the enrolment window requires an out-of-band channel or enterprise identity federation. \emph{Erasure coding.} Reed--Solomon or IDA-style coding~\cite{rabin1989,bessani2011depsky} would lower storage overhead and give true dispersal, at the cost of complexity. \emph{Client-side encryption.} The backend sees plaintext and keys (non-goal~(ii)); end-to-end encryption in the client would remove this but complicates sharing, server-side verification and detection. \emph{HSM-backed KMS.} The local keystore should be replaced by an external KMS or HSM in production; an AWS KMS adapter exists but was exercised only against moto. Finally, timing side channels were not measured, no fuzzing beyond a hand-picked payload list was performed, and there are no React component tests.
 
